<title>USA: Crown Crafts Q4 EPS $0.20, after $0.14 gain.</title>
<headline>Crown Crafts Q4 EPS $0.20, after $0.14 gain.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>CROWN CRAFTS, INC.</p>
<p>					    For the Three Months Ended</p>
<p>				    Mar 30, 1997	   Mar 31, 1996</p>
<p> Net sales			$ 64,250,000	   $ 60,256,000</p>
<p> Net earnings (loss)	     1,628,000		(722,000)</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p>  Primary				   0.20		   (0.09)</p>
<p>  Fully-diluted			   0.20		   (0.09)</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding:</p>
<p>  Primary			    8,191,931		7,944,201</p>
<p>  Fully-diluted		    8,334,102		7,944,201</p>
<p>					    For the Fiscal Years Ended</p>
<p>				    Mar 30, 1997	   Mar 31, 1996</p>
<p> Net sales			$256,385,000	   $219,002,000</p>
<p> Net earnings			3,631,000		3,947,000</p>
<p>Earnings per share:</p>
<p>  Primary				   0.45		     0.49</p>
<p>  Fully-diluted			   0.45		     0.49</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding:</p>
<p>  Primary			    8,006,134		8,125,048</p>
<p>  Fully-diluted		    8,041,676		8,125,048</p>
<p>NOTE: Results for the fourth quarter included year-end adjustments which increased net income by $1.2 million, or $0.14 per share, consisting primarily of a year-end inventory write-up.</p>
<p>Results for fiscal 1997 were reduced by a one-time charge of $1.3 million, or $0.16 per share, as a result of losses from incurred in connectiuon with the third-quarter recall of foal furniture products maufactured by a subsidiary, and for actula and expected costs associated with the company's decision to exit certain product categories.</p>
</text>
